// Coordination service of the Raft KV (00E §5, ADR-002, ADR-005, ADR-006, task 04.01): the
// API the scheduler and the API tier use for leader election, fencing epochs and worker leases.
// It holds coordination state only; Postgres owns workflow state (ADR-003).
//
// Errors are gRPC statuses carrying a google.rpc.ErrorInfo whose reason is a 00E §4 code:
//   - NOT_LEADER (FAILED_PRECONDITION): this node can't serve the request; metadata
//     "leader_hint" is the leader's node id when known. Retry against it.
//   - NO_QUORUM (UNAVAILABLE): a write or linearizable read could not reach a quorum.
//   - CONFLICT (ABORTED): an expected_version did not match; metadata "current_version".
//     (Task 04.01 calls this VERSION_MISMATCH; 00E §4 names version conflicts CONFLICT.)
//   - INVALID_ARGUMENT, NOT_FOUND (an unknown or expired lease), as in 00E §4.
//   - UNAVAILABLE: a timeout or a node going down; the outcome of a write is unknown, so retry
//     it with the same meta (task 04.04).
// When the state machine decided the outcome, metadata "result_code" names its ResultCode
// without the prefix (command.proto), e.g. LEASE_EXPIRED vs LEASE_NOT_FOUND behind NOT_FOUND.
